            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>Thyrotropin (TSH) is mildly elevated above the reference range, which may indicate subclinical or mild primary hypothyroidism. Correlation with clinical symptoms and further assessment of thyroid hormone levels (free T4, free T3) is recommended to clarify thyroid function status, especially considering the patient's advanced age.</td></tr></table></div>"
